  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `xtask/src/heavy_covers.rs` (new): `gate heavy --covers <PR>:<head sha>`. The tool refuses a sha that is not a commit, a head that is not an ancestor of `HEAD`, and a working tree with changes. It prints `covers: #<PR> <sha>` for each head and `tree: <HEAD^{tree}>` in the plan header and under the summary. A real run writes `covers.txt` to the gate log directory: the header, each step with its result and note, the counts, the wall time and the verdict. `--dry-run` prints the header and runs nothing.\n- `xtask/src/gate_args.rs` (new): `GateArgs` and `parse_gate`, moved from `main.rs` with the new repeatable `--covers` flag. The flag applies to the heavy tier only. A bad value, a repeated PR or another tier is a refusal with the usage text. `main.rs` goes from 407 to 344 lines.\n- `xtask/src/main.rs`: the module list, the usage line and the `heavy` arm of `gate()`. With no `--covers`, the behaviour does not change.\n- `xtask/src/heavy_covers_tests.rs` (new): 4 tests.\n- `AGENTS.md` \"Heavy lanes at review\": the PR form and the wave form (#3460). \"Not run\" is never a pass, a PR that merges alone keeps the PR form, and the cut tier stays the final check. A wave record covers a PR only for the head that it names. A safety-floor PR is covered only if the trial tree contains its final head.\n- `.claude/skills/merge-ready/SKILL.md`: new step 4a. It makes the trial tree (a detached worktree under `.claude/worktrees/`, `git merge --no-ff` of each PR head in the planner's order onto `origin/main`, never pushed, removed after the run). It runs the gate one time, gives the one fixed comment form (`<!-- heavy-wave: <tree hash> -->`), and says what to do on a red step and when a head is no longer covered.\n- `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md`: the table row and the wave form bullets.\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`: new section 2e, the two sources of heavy evidence.\n- `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md` step 5: a reviewer accepts a wave record only if its `covers:` line names the current head of the PR, all reached lanes are in it, and its verdict is `PASS`. The reviewer duty of #2568 stays (pinned by `runner_review_requires_heavy_lanes_without_author_results`).\n- `docs/decisions/3460-heavy-run-per-wave.md`: chosen, why, dropped, with the maintainer's words.\n\n## The maintainer's words (#3460, 2026-11-22)\n\n> A wave of PRs that the planner groups together gets ONE heavy run on a trial tree of the wave (current `main` plus each PR of the wave). The result is recorded on each PR of the wave (tree hash, lanes, counts). A red step is attributed to a PR, that PR leaves the wave, and the run starts again for the rest.\n>\n> Rules that stay:\n> - \"Not run\" is never a pass.\n> - A PR that merges alone keeps the rule of today.\n> - The release tier at the cut stays the final check.\n\n> Safety-floor PRs: the wave run covers them only if the trial tree contains their final head.\n\n## Dry run of the flag on this head (fe265cdc2)\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --covers 3460:fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4 --covers 3467:fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4 --dry-run`\n\n```\ncovers: #3460 fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4\ncovers: #3467 fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4\ntree: ad917da9b71262dd58c35ad5032aba1c4a299267\nbase: origin/main 5326584a7abae6ebc35228ad1e871e293c1103c3\nchanged since origin/main: 11 file(s)\nheavy plan (release --ignored lanes the diff reaches, #2568):\n  the diff reaches no heavy lane: nothing to run\n...\n== gate summary (heavy) - logs in ...\\gate-logs\\heavy-20261122-151711\n  wall 0.0 min, 0 step(s), 0 failed\n  covers: #3460 fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4\n  covers: #3467 fe265cdc2a13c015c4db22b32080138fd25163d4\n  tree: ad917da9b71262dd58c35ad5032aba1c4a299267\n  base: origin/main 5326584a7abae6ebc35228ad1e871e293c1103c3\n  planned: 0 step(s), dry run: nothing ran\n  the wave reaches no heavy lane\n```\n\n## Changes after the review (comment 7081027933) and the decision on #3467\n\n- Blocker 1: `--covers` refuses `--only` and `--failed` with the usage text (`gate_args.rs`). The record has `counts: <planned> planned, <ran> ran, <ok> ok, <failed> failed`. The verdict is `INCOMPLETE` when a planned step did not run (`heavy_covers::verdict`). Only `PASS` covers a head.\n- Blocker 2: `merge-ready` step 4a item 10: a `SAME` or `MECHANICAL` refresh keeps the heavy result of a wave-2 PR. A `DELTA` or `NEW CODE` refresh needs a new result (its own run, or a wave record that names the new head). AGENTS.md says the same in the PR form.\n- Note 1: `<!-- heavy-wave: ... -->` is in the AGENTS.md list of fixed strings and in the collaborator-marker rule.\n- Note 2: the header, the summary and `covers.txt` print `base: <ref> <merge-base sha>`. Step 4a item 9: if `origin/main` moved after the run, run the planner again. A PR whose trial merge is no longer clean leaves the wave.\n- Note 3: a plan with no step gives `verdict: NO LANE` and the line \"the wave reaches no heavy lane\", in the tool and in the comment form.\n- #3467 (maintainer decision, 2026-11-22): new stable rule **Owed heavy result** in AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\". A review of a `P3` or lower PR can set `merge-ready` with \"not run - owed to the wave run before merge\" and the owed lanes. The merge waits for a green record that names the final head. A `P1` or `P2` PR (or a PR with no priority label) keeps the strict rule. Text in PR-reviewer step 5 and its review comment line, the `review-prs` skill (2e), the `merge-ready` skill (4a item 11), the `gate` skill and the decision file (second entry, with his words).\n\n> Maintainer decision, 2026-11-22, given in the question dialog: **allowed for P3 and lower only.**\n> - A review of a P3 or lower PR may set `merge-ready` while the heavy result says \"not run - owed to the wave run before merge\". The comment names the owed lanes.\n> - The merge (not the review) waits for a green run that covers the final head, with the `--covers <PR>:<sha>` record of #3460.\n> - A P1 or P2 PR keeps the strict rule: the heavy result on the head comes before the label `merge-ready`.\n> - The coordinator refuses to merge a PR with an owed heavy result until the covering record names the head.\n\n## Tests (head fe265cdc2)\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask -j 6`: `test result: ok. 281 passed; 0 failed` (bin), and all other xtask targets ok.\n- Pinning tests:\n  - `heavy_covers_tests::covers_is_repeatable_on_the_heavy_tier`\n  - `heavy_covers_tests::covers_refuses_other_tiers_and_bad_values` (now also `--covers` with `--only` and `--failed`)\n  - `heavy_covers_tests::header_and_record_name_each_head_the_tree_and_the_counts` (now with the `base:` line and the planned count)\n  - `heavy_covers_tests::not_run_is_never_a_pass_in_the_record` (new: `INCOMPLETE`, `NO LANE`)\n  - `heavy_covers_tests::a_head_that_the_trial_tree_lacks_is_refused` (now also the merge-base sha)\n  - `heavy_plan_tests::an_owed_heavy_result_is_allowed_for_p3_and_lower_only` (new, #3467: P3 and lower can defer with the fixed text; P1 and P2 cannot)\n  - `heavy_plan_tests::runner_review_requires_heavy_lanes_without_author_results` (unchanged, passes)\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -j 6 -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches no heavy lane (dry run above).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real wave run: no heavy lane ran, and no `covers.txt` was written by a real run (the text is pinned by the unit test).\n- The merge-ready step 4a procedure end to end, and the `heavy-wave` comment on real PRs.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3460\nFixes #3467\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
